<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RUT_AridShrubland                              UtinniPatches - authored 2026-09-09
    BIOME_OWNERSHIP_WAVE_1. Full sheet: design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/
    arid_shrubland.md (FROZEN).

    MEASURED (sheet SS0): 665 tiles, arc p10/median/p90 62.1/82.2/102.3 (sun 9.2 deg
    above horizon at the core), temp p10/median/p90 -0.8/19.7/32.1 C, flat core
    (312/361 core tiles). Thematic handle: "the hush," gesture "everything leans
    toward the light."

    Weather is the sheet's whole mechanism: ban 1 is explicit "No rain (planet-wide,
    R-H1). Fog only" — so Rain/RainyThunderstorm/FoggyRain are zeroed and Fog carries
    the biome (SS3 "the only water is fog on that wind"). Snow zeroed to match: the
    sheet names exactly one water source (fog) and nothing else. Clear stays present
    (SS5 "always wind," not always fog) but ban 5 also stands — "No still-air
    baseline... calm exists only as the Stall event" — a wind-hediff/event concern,
    not a weather-commonality field, carried here as a flag rather than a value
    change (no WeatherDef exists yet for the Stall/Gale; SS Owed).

    terrainsByFertility kept at the donor's own Sand/Soil/SoilRich thresholds: the
    sheet's own SS4 "Sand is gone — held down by roots... the ground is root-bound
    crust" reads as a texture/graphic note (ban 7 bans open SAND TERRAIN on core
    tiles), not a threshold change this pass can safely re-author without inventing a
    new TerrainDef; flagged rather than invented.

    wildAnimals/wildPlants: transplanted from BiomeCast_Ashkarr.xml /
    BiomeFlora_Ashkarr.xml against rosters/arid_shrubland.json.

    NOT this pass's scope: the sweetline trees (owner's pick, huge/ancient,
    TREE_GRAPHICS_OWNERSHIP_1); the Stall/Gale WeatherDefs and their AI hooks (SS
    Owed, engine feasibility pass not run); the band-mend repaint
    (WORLDMAP_DESERT_BAND_REPAIR_1).

    COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1 (2026-09-21, arid_shrubland sheet partial pass)
    landed three of that sheet's owed slugs here: `RUT_Fuzz` (the fuzz, wildPlants,
    replacing the Plant_ShrubLow stand-in), `RSW_ShrublandGiant` (the huge grazer
    flagship, life-stage art only - parental enrage is new C#, filed separately)
    and `RSW_TunnelSnake` (the signature corridor predator, alongside the existing
    Terrorworm interim). Names for all three, and for the pre-existing giants/
    snake-analogs/bird-analogs generically, remain the owner's pick
    (ARIDSHRUBLAND_SHIPPING_NAMES_1) - every RUT_/RSW_ defName above added this
    pass is a working name, same status as RUT_Vorrel.

    SHRUBLAND_SCRAPNEST_BIRDS_1 (2026-09-20) added `RSW_ScrapNestBird`, the §4
    scrap-nest bird-analog the tunnel snake's own description already preys on.
    It reuses RSW_Whisperbird's art and flight frames under a new defName and a
    retint, so the four donor birds this file already places (Whisperbird,
    Convor, Porg, Nuna) are untouched and no species is double-booked. Its
    nests (`RSW_ScrapNest`) are built by the birds at runtime, not by map gen,
    so nothing here places them.

    VENOMVINE_FORTRESS_PASSABILITY_1 (2026-09-21) added `RM_VenomvineThicket` to
    wildPlants — §4's "fortress flora", the shrubland lineage of the desert's
    `RM_Venomvine` and the sole carve-out from §6.6's ban on dense flora here. The
    dungeon is the def's own clustering (radius 8, weight 25), NOT a TerrainDef or
    a structure; "small creatures pass through easily; larger ones simply cannot"
    is `RM_CompProperties_BodySizeBarrier` on that def, which makes a thicket cell
    impassable to the pathfinder for anything over BodySize 1.5 — every huge grazer
    on this plain, `RSW_ShrublandGiant` included. Live verification is owed
    (`VENOMVINE_FORTRESS_LIVE_VERIFY_1`).

  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RUT_AridShrubland</defName>
    <label>the arid shrubland</label>
    <description>Knee-high silver-green fuzz at eerily even spacing, running unbroken to every horizon, all of it leaning the same way, all of it moving - because the wind never stops. No rain falls here; the only water is fog carried in on the ground-wind, thinning with every sunward metre. Sightlines are gone under the fuzz-canopy and cover is everywhere, for everything, all the time: the moment the environment stops trying to kill you, the danger becomes each other.</description>
    <workerClass>RimWorld.BiomeWorker_AridShrubland</workerClass>
    <riverbankTerrain>Riverbank</riverbankTerrain>
    <allowRoads>true</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>true</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>false</allowFarmingCamps>
    <animalDensity>1.8</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0.35</plantDensity>
    <forageability>0.5</forageability>
    <movementDifficulty>1</movementDifficulty>
    <texture>World/Biomes/AridShrubland1</texture>
    <diseaseMtbDays>65</diseaseMtbDays>
    <diseases>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_GutWorms</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>60</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_MuscleParasites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>60</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_FibrousMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_SensoryMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalFlu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalPlague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_OrganDecay</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>10</commonality>
      </li>
    </diseases>
    <terrainsByFertility>
      <li>
        <terrain>Sand</terrain>
        <min>-999</min>
        <max>0.45</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>Soil</terrain>
        <min>0.45</min>
        <max>0.9</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>SoilRich</terrain>
        <min>0.9</min>
        <max>999</max>
      </li>
    </terrainsByFertility>
    <baseWeatherCommonalities>
      <Clear>30</Clear>
      <Fog>45</Fog>
      <DryThunderstorm>1</DryThunderstorm>
      <SnowGentle>0</SnowGentle>
      <SnowHard>0</SnowHard>
      <Rain>0</Rain>
      <RainyThunderstorm>0</RainyThunderstorm>
      <FoggyRain>0</FoggyRain>
      <GrayPall MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly">1</GrayPall>
      <Overcast MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">5</Overcast>
    </baseWeatherCommonalities>
    <wildAnimals>
      <FrilledGorg MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">1.0</FrilledGorg>  <!-- frilled gorg - small-runway, keep -->
      <Gorg MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">1.0</Gorg>  <!-- gorg - small-runway, keep -->
      <Iriaz MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">1.0</Iriaz>  <!-- iriaz - small-herd, keep -->
      <LongtailGorg MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">1.0</LongtailGorg>  <!-- longtail gorg - medium-interface, keep -->
      <Eopie MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.8</Eopie>  <!-- eopie - medium-pack, keep -->
      <Kreetle MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.8</Kreetle>  <!-- kreetle - small-runway, keep -->
      <Lothcat MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.8</Lothcat>  <!-- loth-cat - small-runway, keep -->
      <Mudhorn MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.8</Mudhorn>  <!-- mudhorn - huge-predator-exception, keep -->
      <Ronto MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.8</Ronto>  <!-- ronto - huge-grazer, keep -->
      <RSW_ShrublandGiant MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.35</RSW_ShrublandGiant>  <!-- COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1: the huge-grazer flagship, large-young/parental-enrage slug -->
      <RSW_TunnelSnake MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.5</RSW_TunnelSnake>  <!-- COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1: the signature corridor predator, alongside the Terrorworm interim -->
      <RSW_ScrapNestBird MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.45</RSW_ScrapNestBird>  <!-- SHRUBLAND_SCRAPNEST_BIRDS_1: the §4 scrap-nest bird-analog; the tunnel snake's own prey -->
      <Scurrier MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.8</Scurrier>  <!-- scurrier - small-runway, keep -->
      <Sketto MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.8</Sketto>  <!-- sketto - small-runway, keep -->
      <RSW_ImperialToad MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.7</RSW_ImperialToad>  <!-- imperial toad - small-runway, keep -->
      <Terrorworm MayRequire="mlie.horrors">0.7</Terrorworm>  <!-- terrorworm - medium-tunnel, keep -->
      <Igitz MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.7</Igitz>  <!-- igitz - small-runway, keep -->
      <Urusai MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.7</Urusai>  <!-- urusai - medium-interface, keep -->
      <Kybuck MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.6</Kybuck>  <!-- kybuck - medium-runner, keep -->
      <Massiff MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.6</Massiff>  <!-- massiff - medium-interface, keep -->
      <Bantha MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.5</Bantha>  <!-- bantha - huge-grazer, keep -->
      <Pufferpig MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.5</Pufferpig>  <!-- Pufferpig - small-runway, keep -->
      <Anooba MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.4</Anooba>  <!-- anooba - medium-interface, adjust-keep -->
      <Corinathoth MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.4</Corinathoth>  <!-- corinathoth - huge-grazer, keep -->
      <Gizka MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.4</Gizka>  <!-- gizka - small-runway, keep -->
      <Nuna MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.4</Nuna>  <!-- nuna - small-runway, keep -->
      <Worrt MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.4</Worrt>  <!-- worrt - small-runway, keep -->
      <RSW_MossBeetle MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.3</RSW_MossBeetle>  <!-- moss beetle - small-runway, keep -->
      <AA_Cactipine MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.25</AA_Cactipine>  <!-- cactipine - small-venom, keep -->
      <Grank MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.2</Grank>  <!-- Grank - medium-interface, keep -->
      <Qormot MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.2</Qormot>  <!-- qormot - medium-interface, keep -->
      <Strill MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.2</Strill>  <!-- strill - medium-interface, keep -->
      <Cannok MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.16</Cannok>  <!-- cannok - medium-interface, keep -->
      <Whisperbird MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.15</Whisperbird>  <!-- whisperbird - flier-interface, keep -->
      <Pikobis MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.1</Pikobis>  <!-- pikobis - medium-runner, keep -->
      <AA_Needlepost MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.1</AA_Needlepost>  <!-- needlepost - small-venom, adjust-keep -->
      <AA_Wildpawn MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.1</AA_Wildpawn>  <!-- wildpawn - medium-venom, keep -->
      <Convor MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.08</Convor>  <!-- convor - flier-interface, keep -->
      <Skalder MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.08</Skalder>  <!-- skalder - huge-grazer, keep -->
      <Vulptex MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.08</Vulptex>  <!-- vulptex - small-runway, keep -->
      <FeralNerf MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.04</FeralNerf>  <!-- feral nerf - medium-runner, keep -->
      <Porg MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.04</Porg>  <!-- porg - small-runway, keep -->
      <AA_Wildpod MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.025</AA_Wildpod>  <!-- wildpod - huge-sessile, keep -->
      <Voorpak MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.02</Voorpak>  <!-- voorpak - small-runway, keep -->
      <KowakianMonkeyLizard MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.01</KowakianMonkeyLizard>  <!-- kowakian monkey-lizard - small-runway, keep -->
    </wildAnimals>
    <coastalWildAnimals />
    <wildPlants>
      <RUT_Fuzz MayRequire="mandrake.rut.ashkarrflora">0.9</RUT_Fuzz>  <!-- COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1: the fuzz def landed, replaces the Plant_ShrubLow stand-in -->
      <RG_Plant_AridGrass>0.5</RG_Plant_AridGrass>  <!-- grass -->
      <Plant_Brambles>0.3</Plant_Brambles>  <!-- brambles -->
      <RUT_Grellbush MayRequire="mandrake.rut.ashkarrflora">0.3</RUT_Grellbush>  <!-- DESERT_FAMILY_PORT_EXECUTION_1 owner ruling 2026-09-21: our own def, replaces vanilla Plant_Bush -->
      <RUT_Grellspine MayRequire="mandrake.rut.ashkarrflora">0.3</RUT_Grellspine>  <!-- DESERT_FAMILY_PORT_EXECUTION_1 owner ruling 2026-09-21: our own def, replaces Biotech's Plant_Ripthorn -->
      <RUT_WildHealroot MayRequire="mandrake.rut.ashkarrflora">0.25</RUT_WildHealroot>  <!-- DESERT_FAMILY_PORT_EXECUTION_1 owner ruling 2026-09-21: our own def, replaces vanilla Plant_HealrootWild. Label kept "wild healroot" per PlantNames_Ashkarr.xml (owner 2026-09-05: healroot is already an invented word, not renamed) -->
      <Plant_Nysyllin_Wild>0.22</Plant_Nysyllin_Wild>  <!-- wild nysyllin plant -->
      <RG_Plant_CreepStern>0.2</RG_Plant_CreepStern>  <!-- creep stern -->
      <RG_Plant_CrimsonCushion>0.2</RG_Plant_CrimsonCushion>  <!-- crimson cushion -->
      <RG_Plant_Dervish>0.2</RG_Plant_Dervish>  <!-- dervish -->
      <RM_VenomvineThicket MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">0.15</RM_VenomvineThicket>  <!-- the fortress flora, §4 — VENOMVINE_FORTRESS_PASSABILITY_1. Lowest weight in this list on purpose and it is NOT a density dial: §4 says thickets "sometimes manage to colonize" and §6.6 bans dense flora here with this as the sole carve-out, so what must stay rare is the NUMBER of stands. How solid each one is comes from wildClusterRadius 8 / wildClusterWeight 25 on the def, not from this weight — raising this scatters more islands rather than thickening the ones there are. -->
    </wildPlants>
    <wildPlantRegrowDays>27</wildPlantRegrowDays>
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
